[size=5][b]NPC Pathing NG[/b][/size]
[size=3]Version [b]3.0.0[/b] · Source: [url=https://github.com/SenjuWoo/Modern-NPC-Pathing]GitHub[/url][/size]

[b]Unsticks NPCs.[/b] Stuck NPCs that are actually trying to walk hurdle fences, vault ledges and drop down on their own, or climb with SkyParkour and EVG Animated Traversal markers when those are installed, and only then use a short validated last-resort teleport. Built on the current CommonLibSSE-NG: one DLL for Skyrim SE 1.5.97, AE 1.6.x and 1.7.x. [b]Detects Fluid Motion and NpcTraversalNG (Enemies Can Jump and Vault) and lets them go first.[/b]

[size=4][b]One installer, nothing to choose[/b][/size]
The FOMOD has no pages. The plugin detects SkyParkour, EVG, Fluid Motion, FluidMotionNPC and NpcTraversalNG when the game starts; the installer adds the SkyParkour-aware StepUpOnto SKSE build only if StepUpOnto is installed.

[size=4][b]What this mod does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Detects NPCs that are [b]trying to walk[/b] but not moving (idle/sandbox/sit/swim/mount/dialogue ignored)
[*][b]Own hurdle / vault / drop[/b] for humanoids: collision-checked arc, vanilla jump animations, no animation files and no SkyParkour needed
[*]Optional [b]SkyParkour[/b] vault/climb, [b]follower replay[/b] of your moves, [b]EVG markers as routes[/b]
[*][b]Compatibility layer[/b]: an NPC that Fluid Motion or NpcTraversalNG is moving is never touched; the own leap switches off while they own jumps; this mod waits twice as long and acts as the fallback
[*]Doorway-aware handling; validated last-resort teleport (disableable)
[*][b]Frame budget[/b]: heavy work is queued and capped per frame (MCM slider)
[*]MCM via MCM Helper, or INI without it
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility mode[/b][/size]
MCM > NPC Pathing NG > Compatibility: [b]Auto[/b] (default), [b]Always run own traversal[/b], [b]Passive[/b]. The log lists exactly what was detected.

[size=4][b]What this mod does NOT claim[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Not a full AI or pathfinding overhaul
[*]The own leap is humanoid-only; creatures and brutes are NpcTraversalNG's job
[*]Default max climb is [b]130[/b] units; indoor parkour/leaps are off by default
[*]SkyParkour climb sounds are 2D: NPCs farther than [b]1600[/b] units will not parkour
[*]3.0.0 was compiled, unit-tested and package-verified but [b]not yet played[/b]; if it crashes on load, roll back to 2.5.0 and send NPCPathingNG.log
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[b]Required[/b]
[list]
[*]Skyrim SE (1.5.97) or AE (1.6.x / 1.7.x)
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[/list]

[b]Optional[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/132292]SkyParkour V3[/url] + Nemesis/Pandora behavior patch
[*]SkyUI + [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/53000]MCM Helper[/url]
[*]EVG Animated Traversal
[*]Fluid Motion and/or NpcTraversalNG: detected, never required
[/list]

No Visual C++ Redistributable needed. The plugin is ESL-flagged.

[size=4][b]Upgrading[/b][/size]
Install over 2.x. Existing globals and FormIDs are unchanged; three globals were added, which is safe on an existing save. Saves keep their MCM values.
